  "summary": "Four supplied studies directly use multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling for identifying fraudulent transactions. [V0068] is strongest on a detection metric (GridWatch; F1=0.89), followed by [V0067] (ToxiBench; AUROC=0.82). [V0065] reports LedgerGuard accuracy=0.68, while [V0066] reports CellLife test MAE=0.75; these are not directly comparable because accuracy/F1/AUROC are higher-is-better whereas MAE is lower-is-better. Prior-work-only mentions in [V0152], [V0103], [V0141], and [V0142] are not counted as applications. The fifth ID [V0069] is included only to satisfy the requested five-ID format: it is fraud-topic but uses representation learning with paired positive and negative examples on LedgerGuard (test MAE=0.79), not the requested hierarchical Bayesian method.",
